(at least for the time being), that ping works better. I do get this,

though:

$ ping -c 3 gw

PING gw.local (192.168.1.254) from 192.168.1.2 : 56(84) bytes of data.

64 bytes from gw.local (192.168.1.254): icmp_seq=0 ttl=255 time=442 usec

